{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Yehi</b>: \"the poor\" — like פס ידא (the palm of a hand). \"Bar\" is like כף זורעת בר (a handful sowing grain), or: on the tops of mountains. And וירעש: this is the fruit, which is the בר. And the meaning: that it be great, shaking like the trees of Lebanon." "<b>Ve-yatzitzu me-ir</b>: like \"from a city\" — the opposite of והנותר בבשר ובלחם (and what remains of flesh and bread). And some say: כי בר, like כבור ידי, and it has no meaning."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 72, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:03.693363697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}